Note: Phase 45 REQ-BEAT-TEST-02 — default IDENTITY behavior across timesigs.
Note: NO `enable beat-true-to-sig;` — pragma OFF means the multiplier is ALWAYS
Note: 1.0, so `1b` prints "1" in EVERY meter (even 6/8 and 2/2). This is the
Note: surprise-free default for scripts that never opt in (D-02 / D-10).

use "@std"

Note: 4/4 — denom=4, pragma off → identity
tempo 120 {
  timesig 4/4 {
    Beat a = 1b
    (print (str a))
  }
}

Note: 6/8 — pragma off → STILL identity (no retune to eighth-beat unit)
tempo 120 {
  timesig 6/8 {
    Beat b = 1b
    (print (str b))
  }
}

Note: 2/2 cut time — pragma off → STILL identity (no retune to half-beat unit)
tempo 120 {
  timesig 2/2 {
    Beat c = 1b
    (print (str c))
  }
}

(print "test_beat_pragma_off: PASSED")
